      "worked_solution": "The maximum value of the parabola is the $y$-coordinate of the vertex of the parabola. \n\nRemember that the vertex form of a parabola is\n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=-(x-2)^{2}+5\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=2$ and $k=5.$ Therefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(2,5),$ and its maximum value is $5.$",
